; bfsodium KDF_CTR_SHA_256 : NIST SP 800_108r1 section 4 1  counter mode
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The pseudorandom function is sha256/hmac  PASTED  and
; entered once per thirty two bytes of output; The counter is stepped by
; chacha20/add32  PASTED  rather than by a ripple written out here  because a
; proved adder is cheaper to trust than a fifth hand rolled carry;
;
; As in sha256/hashcore  a run of ONE repeated token is a repetition rather
; than a decision and is written as such; every offset and every branch below
; was worked out from the map and written down;
;
; IO  in:  klen{2} LE  fixedlen{2} LE  okmlen{2} LE  kbuf{256}  fixedbuf{256}
;     out: okm{okmlen}
;
; Only the first klen bytes of the key buffer are looked at  and the same for
; the fixed input; the rest MUST be nought;
;
; THE COUNTER IS THIRTY TWO BITS AND COMES FIRST  which is the arrangement
; CAVP tests and the one callers in the wild use; SP 800_108 allows eight
; sixteen twenty four or thirty two  and a width chosen at run time is not
; available here: the fixed input would start at a cell whose address the
; width decides  and this library has no index; So the width is FIXED at
; thirty two and stated  rather than taken as an argument that would have to
; be honoured by sliding;
;
; THE STANDARD LEAVES THE FIXED INPUT TO THE CALLER  conventionally Label then
; a nought byte then Context then the wanted length in bits; this routine
; takes it as one blob and does not assemble it  because assembling it would
; assert a layout the standard does not fix  and because CAVP hands it over
; as one blob too;
;
; FIXEDLEN IS AT MOST A HUNDRED AND EIGHTY EIGHT  and the reason is one level
; down: sha256/hmac takes at most a hundred and ninety two bytes from memory
; because sha256/hashcore's prefix buffer is two hundred and fifty six and the
; key pad block takes a quarter of it; four of those hundred and ninety two
; are the counter;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  klen{2}      u16 LE  the key's length
;   @0x002:0x003  fixedlen{2}  u16 LE  the fixed input's length
;   @0x004:0x005  okmlen{2}    u16 LE  how many bytes are wanted
;   @0x006:0x105  kbuf{256}    u8      the key  as given
;   @0x106:0x205  fixedbuf{256} u8     the fixed input  as given
;   @0x206:0x305  ktemp{256}   u8      hands the key back after a copy
;   @0x306:0x405  ftemp{256}   u8      hands the fixed input back after a copy
;   @0x408:0x41b  the adder frame; chacha20/add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x408
;                 its a{4} IS THE COUNTER  little endian  and its b{4} at
;                 @0x40c is the one the counter steps by
;   @0x41c:0x41f  ctmp{4}      hands the counter back after a copy
;   @0x420:0x427  owedlo owedhi chances flag test back and two spare cells
;                 the counts are tested and handed back through
;   @0x428:0x447  K{32}        this turn's PRF output  written out and spent
;   @0x450:0xb5b  sha256/hmac's frame  pasted at @0x450; footprint 0:1803
;
; THE COUNT STILL OWED IS KEPT WHERE IT IS TESTED; okmlen arrives at @0x004
; and moves into the counts frame before the first turn  because the test runs
; once per byte written out and a walk of a thousand cells each time would
; cost more than the hash it is counting;
;
; Nothing buffers the output; each K is written as it is made and the last is
; cut short  so the tape does not grow with the length asked for;
;
; A digest is a byte string and hmac leaves its answer as eight little endian
; words  so the copy into K reverses each word; that is the same boundary
; sha256/hmac documents and gets wrong at its peril;

; read the three lengths and the two buffers
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
